    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0336" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Argentina/435: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-14T18:00:00-03:00">December 14, 1942—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2547. For Ducas,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d319-f1"/> USCCo, from Albarracin.<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d319-f2"/> Embassy reliably informed that small quantities
                    platinum intended for Axis are now being purchased in Colombia through Argentine
                    channels. Informant who entirely trustworthy assures Embassy he can purchase 5
                    kilos now on hand and arrange purchase 2 kilos monthly thereafter payment
                    against delivery Embassy Bogotá or designee. Price about 18 Argentine pesos gram
                    including informant’s travel expenses here to Colombia as his presence there
                    essential.</p>
                <p>This would stop at source part supply now coming here for Axis. Please cable if
                    you wish us arrange. [Albarracin.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d319-f1" n="38" xml:id="d319-f1-content">
                <p>Robert N. Ducas, Executive Vice President of the United States Commercial
                    Company.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d319-f2" n="39" xml:id="d319-f2-content">
                <p>Louis A. Albarracin, field representative of the United States Commercial
                    Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
